menu "Lector Arduino TinyUSB bridge"
    config TINYUSB_ENABLED
        bool
        default y
        depends on TINYUSB_MSC_ENABLED
        help
            On wherever esp_tinyusb's MSC is (env:x4pro, USB Drive). The Arduino
            core then builds USB.cpp, USBMSC.cpp and esp32-hal-tinyusb.c against
            esp_tinyusb; without it USBMSC.cpp does not compile once
            CONFIG_TINYUSB_MSC_ENABLED is set. Lector's core rebuild has no
            lib-builder arduino_tinyusb component; this one stands in for it.
            No prompt, so the lib-builder sdkconfig's CONFIG_TINYUSB_ENABLED=y
            cannot turn it on in envs without esp_tinyusb.
endmenu
